# Filament Performance
- Eager-load every relationship a table column, infolist entry, or action touches via `->modifyQueryUsing(fn ($q) => $q->with([...]))` or `with()` in `getEloquentQuery()`; dot-notation columns (`author.name`) lazy-load per row otherwise.
- Use `->counts()`, `->exists()`, `->sum()` column shortcuts instead of accessors or closures that query per row.
- Mark `searchable()`/`sortable()` only on indexed columns; searching computed or unindexed columns requires an index or dedicated search backend first.
- Always paginate tables; never `->paginated(false)` on unbounded datasets; keep per-page options bounded.
- Select only needed columns with `modifyQueryUsing` on wide tables — retain the primary/foreign keys relationships require.
- Defer heavy work: `->deferLoading()` on tables, lazy widgets (`$isLazy = true`), sparing poll intervals, cache expensive stats queries.
- `Select::relationship()` over large tables must be `searchable()` with a bounded `optionsLimit`, never fully hydrated.
